From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chris Blake <chrisrblake93@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 15:44:02 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] rockchip: rk3308: hand the OTP to the non-secure controller
 on RK3308B-S

The RK3308B-S has a different OTP controller than the RK3308 and
RK3308B. Its OTP macro is shared between a secure and a non-secure
controller, selected by bit 2 of SGRF_SOC_CON1. Unless that bit is
cleared, the non-secure controller never leaves standby and every read
returns 0xff.

The SGRF is only writable from the secure world, so clear the bit in
SPL when the GRF chip ID reports an RK3308B-S.

Signed-off-by: Chris Blake <chrisrblake93@gmail.com>
---
 arch/arm/mach-rockchip/rk3308/rk3308.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm/mach-rockchip/rk3308/rk3308.c b/arch/arm/mach-rockchip/rk3308/rk3308.c
index 165abea5..a0eb7c7e 100644
--- a/arch/arm/mach-rockchip/rk3308/rk3308.c
+++ b/arch/arm/mach-rockchip/rk3308/rk3308.c
@@ -128,6 +128,13 @@ int arch_cpu_init(void)
 	/* Set CRYPTO SDMMC EMMC NAND SFC USB master bus to be secure access */
 	rk_clrreg(&sgrf->con_secure0, 0x2b83);
 
+	/*
+	 * RK3308B-S: give the OTP to the non-secure OTP controller, otherwise
+	 * it never leaves standby and every read returns 0xff.
+	 */
+	if (readl(&grf->chip_id) == 0x3308c)
+		rk_clrreg(&sgrf->soc_con1, BIT(2));
+
 	/*
 	 * Enable plus options to use more pinctrl functions, including
 	 * GPIO2A2_PLUS, GPIO2A3_PLUS and I2C3_MULTI_SRC_PLUS.
